<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Petru I of Moldavia</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. c. 1391</span> · Also known as Petru Mușat</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Petru I of Moldavia, known as Petru Mușat, was Prince of Moldavia from about 1375 until about 1391 and the first prince of the Mușatin dynasty. He issued the first Moldavian coins, did homage to King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/w-adys-aw-ii-jagie-o">Władysław II Jagiełło</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poland">Poland</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lviv">Lviv</a> in 1387 to counter Hungarian pressure, and moved the princely court to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/suceava">Suceava</a>, giving the young principality its first lasting institutions.</p></div>
